---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BiodiversityExplorer from '../components/biodiversity/BiodiversityExplorer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Biodiversity" description="Live biodiversity sightings and birds at Tamarind Valley Collective." image="/images/pages/trekking/watering-hole.jpg" imageWidth={1384} imageHeight={1038}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="The TVC Ecosystem" title="What lives here" intro="From over 100 bird species in the food forest itself — explore live sightings below, filed alongside everything else we know about the land's ecosystem." image="/images/pages/trekking/watering-hole.jpg" imageAlt="A forest watering hole on the property, where wildlife comes to drink" />

  <section class="section wrapper">
    <h2>Part of a working wildlife corridor</h2>
    <p>TVC sits inside the Melagiris' elephant corridor — the link between Bannerghatta National Park and the Cauvery that also threads through MM Hills, BR Hills, Sathyamangalam, and the Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve. Part of the range became the Cauvery North Wildlife Sanctuary in 2014, and the dry-deciduous and semi-evergreen habitat it protects is home to elephants, gaur, leopards, and four-horned antelope, alongside the birdlife below. That connectivity is exactly why fragmentation here — farms, roads, settlements — is such a sensitive issue: it's what keeps a corridor a corridor instead of a bottleneck.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrapper">
    <BiodiversityExplorer />
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="wrapper">
      <a class="card geography-card" href="/ecosystem/geography">
        <h3>Weather</h3>
        <p>The land TVC sits on, and the rainfall and monsoon patterns that shape it — including live-updated monthly rainfall.</p>
        <span class="geography-card__link">See the weather →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .geography-card {
    display: block;
    max-width: 480px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .geography-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .geography-card p {
    color: var(--tvc-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .geography-card__link {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--tvc-green-dark);
  }
</style>
